            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of non-small cell lung cancer presenting with renal angle pain and hematuria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>671-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 53-year-old woman was referred urgently to the urology department with a history of worsening right renal angle pain and associated hematuria. Further investigations revealed the presence of a primary non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) invading the posterior chest wall with an associated vaginal metastasis. To our knowledge, this is only the second case report in the literature of a vaginal metastasis from NSCLC.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
